exports[`golden reports from recordings > rabbitmq-3.13/full en 80 columns 1`] = `
"From snapshot taken 2026-10-04 07:31 UTC (context sut)
RabbitMQ 3.13.7 · 1 node · Mnesia
Sources: HTTP API [ok] · management stats [ok] · Prometheus [ok]
10 queues · 19 exchanges · 2 vhosts

S1  DATA SAFETY (2)

  L3  queue overlap
      Several policies match; only one applies
      What happened  Policy overlap-a applies; overlap-b also match and are
                     ignored.
      Is data safe   No. Keys dead-letter-exchange set in an ignored policy have
                     no effect, so this object runs without them.
      Do next        Merge the keys into one policy, or change the patterns so
                     the policies do not overlap.
                     ocho explain L3
      Evidence       observed: http:/api/policies =
                     {"overlap-a":{"max-length":1000}}
                     observed: http:/api/policies =
                     {"overlap-b":{"dead-letter-exchange":"events.unrouted"}}
      Why            RabbitMQ applies a single policy, the one with the highest
                     priority, and never merges keys from other matching
                     policies.

  T5  queue orders.created (vhost payments)
      Dead-lettering can lose messages
      What happened  Dead-letter strategy is at-most-once from default, with
                     overflow drop-head from default.
      Is data safe   No. A dead-lettered message can be lost before it reaches
                     the parking-lot.
      Do next        Set dead-letter-strategy at-least-once and overflow
                     reject-publish together.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost 'payments' policies declare --name
                     'orders-limit' --pattern '^orders\\.' --apply-to 'queues'
                     --priority '0' --definition
                     '{"dead-letter-exchange":"ocho.retry","dead-letter-strategy":"at-least-once","delivery-limit":10,"max-length":100000,"overflow":"reject-publish"}'
                     ocho explain T5
      Evidence       observed: dead-letter-exchange = orders.dlx (argument)
                     inferred: dead-letter-strategy = at-most-once (builtin
                     default)
                     inferred: overflow = drop-head (builtin default)
      Why            At-least-once dead-lettering needs overflow reject-publish;
                     without it the broker silently falls back to at-most-once.

S3  OPERABILITY (13)

  C1  consumer amq.ctag-tsNXWWpmGQy0E4p2b-vYgA on channel conn-a8d568a3ae
      Consumer acknowledges automatically
      What happened  A consumer on queue work.classic, connection
                     conn-59945cd190, uses automatic acknowledgement.
      Is data safe   No. A message is removed as soon as it is sent, so a
                     consumer crash loses it.
      Do next        Switch this consumer to manual ack, sent after the work is
                     committed.
                     ocho explain C1
      Evidence       observed: http:/api/consumers#ackRequired = false

  C2  consumer amq.ctag-tsNXWWpmGQy0E4p2b-vYgA on channel conn-a8d568a3ae
      Consumer prefetch is unbounded or 1
      What happened  A consumer on queue work.classic has prefetch 0.
      Is data safe   Yes. Nothing is lost; prefetch 0 can exhaust consumer
                     memory, and prefetch 1 limits throughput.
      Do next        Set prefetch on this consumer to a measured value, such as
                     20 to 100.
                     ocho explain C2
      Evidence       observed: http:/api/consumers#prefetch = 0

  DX2 node rabbit@host-7e65bb98a3
      Disk free limit is below node memory
      What happened  Node has disk_free_limit 50000000 bytes and a memory limit
                     of 3287213670 bytes.
      Is data safe   Not known. The disk can fill before the broker blocks
                     publishers, and a full disk can lose messages.
      Do next        Set disk_free_limit to at least the memory limit of the
                     node, for example disk_free_limit.relative = 1.0.
                     ocho explain DX2
      Evidence       observed: http:/api/nodes#disk_free_limit = 50,000,000
                     observed: http:/api/nodes#mem_limit = 3,287,213,670

  R1  channel conn-0bb366c774
      Messages are published without confirms
      What happened  A channel on connection conn-61c80d6f3c, user ocho-admin,
                     published 153 messages without publisher confirms.
      Is data safe   Not known. The publisher cannot tell whether the broker
                     took each message.
      Do next        Enable publisher confirms on this channel and wait for them
                     before treating a publish as done.
                     ocho explain R1
      Evidence       observed: http:/api/channels#message_stats.publish = 153
                     observed: http:/api/channels#confirm = false

  T1  queue work.backlog
      Durable data sits in a classic queue
      What happened  This classic queue holds 118 messages and has 1 consumer.
      Is data safe   Not known. A classic queue lives on one node; if that node
                     loses its disk, the messages are lost.
      Do next        Move this queue to a quorum queue through a migration.
                     ocho explain T1
      Evidence       inferred: derived:queue.type = classic

  T2  exchange direct
      Unroutable messages can be dropped
      What happened  This exchange has no usable alternate exchange (missing); a
                     message that matches no binding is dropped.
      Is data safe   Not known. No drop is counted yet, but the next message
                     that matches no binding is lost.
      Do next        Set an alternate exchange on this exchange through a
                     policy; the fanout exchange ocho.unroutable and its queue
                     must exist first.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost '/' policies declare --name
                     'ocho-ae-direct' --pattern '^direct$' --apply-to
                     'exchanges' --priority '0' --definition
                     '{"alternate-exchange":"ocho.unroutable"}'
                     ocho explain T2
      Evidence       observed: alternate-exchange = not set
                     inferred: derived:binding.destination = 3

  T2  exchange orders (vhost payments)
      Unroutable messages can be dropped
      What happened  This exchange has no usable alternate exchange (missing); a
                     message that matches no binding is dropped.
      Is data safe   Not known. No drop is counted yet, but the next message
                     that matches no binding is lost.
      Do next        Set an alternate exchange on this exchange through a
                     policy; the fanout exchange ocho.unroutable and its queue
                     must exist first.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost 'payments' policies declare --name
                     'ocho-ae-orders' --pattern '^orders$' --apply-to
                     'exchanges' --priority '0' --definition
                     '{"alternate-exchange":"ocho.unroutable"}'
                     ocho explain T2
      Evidence       observed: alternate-exchange = not set
                     inferred: derived:binding.destination = 1

  T3  queue overlap
      A full queue drops its oldest messages
      What happened  Queue has a length limit of 1000 messages, with overflow
                     drop-head from default.
      Is data safe   No. When the queue is full, the broker deletes messages
                     from its head to make room.
      Do next        Set overflow to reject-publish or reject-publish-dlx
                     through a policy.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost '/' policies declare --name
                     'overlap-a' --pattern '^overlap$' --apply-to 'queues'
                     --priority '2' --definition
                     '{"max-length":1000,"overflow":"reject-publish"}'
                     ocho explain T3
      Evidence       observed: max-length = 1,000 (policy overlap-a)
                     inferred: overflow = drop-head (builtin default)

  T3  queue orders.created (vhost payments)
      A full queue drops its oldest messages
      What happened  Queue has a length limit of 100000 messages, with overflow
                     drop-head from default.
      Is data safe   No. When the queue is full, the broker deletes messages
                     from its head to make room.
      Do next        Set overflow to reject-publish or reject-publish-dlx
                     through a policy.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost 'payments' policies declare --name
                     'orders-limit' --pattern '^orders\\.' --apply-to 'queues'
                     --priority '0' --definition
                     '{"dead-letter-exchange":"ocho.retry","dead-letter-strategy":"at-least-once","delivery-limit":10,"max-length":100000,"overflow":"reject-publish"}'
                     ocho explain T3
      Evidence       observed: max-length = 100,000 (policy orders-limit)
                     inferred: overflow = drop-head (builtin default)

  T3  queue orders.parking (vhost payments)
      A full queue drops its oldest messages
      What happened  Queue has a length limit of 100000 messages, with overflow
                     drop-head from default.
      Is data safe   No. When the queue is full, the broker deletes messages
                     from its head to make room.
      Do next        Set overflow to reject-publish or reject-publish-dlx
                     through a policy.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost 'payments' policies declare --name
                     'orders-limit' --pattern '^orders\\.' --apply-to 'queues'
                     --priority '0' --definition
                     '{"dead-letter-exchange":"ocho.retry","dead-letter-strategy":"at-least-once","delivery-limit":10,"max-length":100000,"overflow":"reject-publish"}'
                     ocho explain T3
      Evidence       observed: max-length = 100,000 (policy orders-limit)
                     inferred: overflow = drop-head (builtin default)

  T4  queue orders.parking (vhost payments)
      Poison messages can be dropped silently
      What happened  Quorum queue has no dead-letter exchange and no delivery
                     limit.
      Is data safe   Yes. Nothing is dropped, but a poison message is
                     redelivered forever and blocks the queue.
      Do next        Set a delivery limit, a dead-letter exchange, at-least-once
                     dead-lettering and overflow reject-publish together through
                     a policy.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost 'payments' policies declare --name
                     'orders-limit' --pattern '^orders\\.' --apply-to 'queues'
                     --priority '0' --definition
                     '{"dead-letter-exchange":"ocho.retry","dead-letter-strategy":"at-least-once","delivery-limit":10,"max-length":100000,"overflow":"reject-publish"}'
                     ocho explain T4
      Evidence       observed: dead-letter-exchange = not set
                     observed: delivery-limit = not set
                     observed: derived:broker.version = 3.13.7

  T9  queue audit
      Expired messages are deleted, not dead-lettered
      What happened  Queue has message-ttl 86400000 ms from policy audit-ttl and
                     no dead-letter exchange.
      Is data safe   No. Expired messages are deleted.
      Do next        Add a dead-letter exchange through a policy, or remove the
                     TTL.
                     rabbitmqadmin --vhost '/' policies declare --name
                     'audit-ttl' --pattern '^audit$' --apply-to 'queues'
                     --priority '1' --definition
                     '{"dead-letter-exchange":"ocho.retry","message-ttl":86400000}'
                     ocho explain T9
      Evidence       observed: message-ttl = 86,400,000 (policy audit-ttl)
                     observed: dead-letter-exchange = not set

  VT3 broker
      Deprecated features are in use
      What happened  The broker reports deprecated feature
                     classic_queue_mirroring in use.
      Is data safe   Yes. Nothing is lost now, but a later version can refuse or
                     remove these features.
      Do next        Plan to stop using each listed feature before the next
                     upgrade.
                     ocho explain VT3
      Evidence       observed: http:/api/deprecated-features/used =
                     classic_queue_mirroring

Not checked (9): Q3 x9 connections · http:/api/users is not available · Enable
                 http:/api/users on the broker

Not visible from the broker: LE2, LE5, LE6, LE10 (client) · LE14, LE17 (lint) ·
                             LE20 (decide) · LE8, LE19 (no tool) · ocho explain
                             LE2

Do these first:
  1. Make dead-lettering at-least-once on queue orders.created (vhost payments)
     (T5)
     ocho explain T5
  2. Merge overlapping policies on queue overlap (L3)
     ocho explain L3
  3. Set overflow reject-publish on queue orders.created (vhost payments), queue
     orders.parking (vhost payments) (T3)
     ocho explain T3

20 rules · 15 fail · 110 pass · 9 not checked · 0 n/a · exit 1
"
